  "outcomes": {
    "primary": [
      {
        "description": "This questionnaire will be used to asses disability. It comprises of 10 items; 7 related to daily living activities; 2 related to pain and 1 related to concentration. Each item is scored from 0 to 5. Total score is expressed as a percentage, with higher scores related to greater disability. Minimum detectable change measurements vary from 4.2 to 13.4, and minimum clinically important differences vary from 5 and 9.5",
        "measure": "Disability Index (DNI)",
        "time_frame": "6th week"
      },
      {
        "description": "Craniovertebral angle can be measured with Image J software. If the angle is less than 50 degrees (\\< 50 degree). The angle will be between tragus of the ear to cervical spinous process C7.",
